<article class="card apx" id="epC" data-n="C" data-search="c error decoder every red message you&#x27;ll see in output, translated into plain english with the fix. errors debugging troubleshooting the errors you will actually hit error message what it means how to fix it attempt to index nil with &#x27;x&#x27; you wrote something.x but something is nil the object doesn&#x27;t exist yet or the name is misspelled. use :waitforchild() or :findfirstchild() and check for nil first. attempt to call a nil value you called a function that doesn&#x27;t exist typo in the function name, or the function is defined below the line that calls it. attempt to perform arithmetic on a nil value math on something that&#x27;s nil a variable was never set, or tonumber() failed. print the value to see. attempt to perform arithmetic on a string value used + to join text use .. for strings, + for numbers. attempt to compare number with nil x &gt; y where one side is nil check both sides exist before comparing. expected &#x27;end&#x27; (to close &#x27;function&#x27; at line n) a missing end every if , for , while , and function needs one end . indent properly and count them. infinite yield possible on &#x27;x:waitforchild(&quot;y&quot;)&#x27; waiting 5+ seconds for something it&#x27;s a warning, not an error. the name is wrong, or you&#x27;re waiting on the wrong parent, or the object is server-only. unable to cast value to object assigned the wrong type e.g. part.parent = &quot;workspace&quot; (a string) instead of workspace . unable to cast double to vector3 gave a number where a vector3 goes part.size = 5 should be part.size = vector3.new(5,5,5) . script timeout: exhausted allowed execution time a loop with no yield add task.wait() inside your while true do . expected &#x27;:&#x27; not &#x27;.&#x27; calling member function used a dot where a colon belongs part:destroy() , not part.destroy() . x is not a valid member of y that child or property doesn&#x27;t exist check spelling and capitalization in explorer. it&#x27;s case-sensitive. players.x.playergui.… is not a valid member client ran before the gui replicated use :waitforchild() in localscripts. attempt to index a nil value (field &#x27;leaderstats&#x27;) leaderstats doesn&#x27;t exist for that player check the folder is named exactly leaderstats and created on playeradded. nothing happens, no error at all the script never ran wrong script type for its location, the script is disabled, or you set no parent on a new instance. debugging checklist is the output window open ? half of all &quot;no error&quot; reports are an unread error. is the script the right type for where it lives? (episode 1 table.) is disabled ticked in the script&#x27;s properties? add print(&quot;reached line 12&quot;) at several points to see how far execution gets. print the suspicious variable itself: print(&quot;part is:&quot;, part) . if it says nil, you found it. check spelling and capitalization against explorer — luau is case-sensitive. did you set parent on anything you created with instance.new ? are you editing while the game is running? press stop first. set a breakpoint by clicking the gutter next to a line number, then play and step through."><header class="chead"><label class="done"><input type="checkbox" class="dchk"><span></span></label><button class="ctoggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="badge apxb">C</span><span class="ctitles"><span class="ctitle">Error decoder</span><span class="ctag">Every red message you&#x27;ll see in Output, translated into plain English with the fix.</span></span><span class="cmeta">reference</span><span class="caret" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span></button></header><div class="cbody"><div class="cinner"><div class="chips"><span class="chip">errors</span><span class="chip">debugging</span><span class="chip">troubleshooting</span></div><h3 class="bh">The errors you will actually hit</h3><div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Error message</th><th>What it means</th><th>How to fix it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>attempt to index nil with 'X'</code></td><td>You wrote <code>something.X</code> but <code>something</code> is nil</td><td>The object doesn't exist yet or the name is misspelled. Use <code>:WaitForChild()</code> or <code>:FindFirstChild()</code> and check for nil first.</td></tr><tr><td><code>attempt to call a nil value</code></td><td>You called a function that doesn't exist</td><td>Typo in the function name, or the function is defined <i>below</i> the line that calls it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>attempt to perform arithmetic on a nil value</code></td><td>Math on something that's nil</td><td>A variable was never set, or <code>tonumber()</code> failed. Print the value to see.</td></tr><tr><td><code>attempt to perform arithmetic on a string value</code></td><td>Used <code>+</code> to join text</td><td>Use <code>..</code> for strings, <code>+</code> for numbers.</td></tr><tr><td><code>attempt to compare number with nil</code></td><td><code>x &gt; y</code> where one side is nil</td><td>Check both sides exist before comparing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Expected 'end' (to close 'function' at line N)</code></td><td>A missing <code>end</code></td><td>Every <code>if</code>, <code>for</code>, <code>while</code>, and <code>function</code> needs one <code>end</code>. Indent properly and count them.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Infinite yield possible on 'X:WaitForChild("Y")'</code></td><td>Waiting 5+ seconds for something</td><td>It's a warning, not an error. The name is wrong, or you're waiting on the wrong parent, or the object is server-only.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Unable to cast value to Object</code></td><td>Assigned the wrong type</td><td>e.g. <code>part.Parent = "workspace"</code> (a string) instead of <code>workspace</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Unable to cast double to Vector3</code></td><td>Gave a number where a Vector3 goes</td><td><code>part.Size = 5</code> should be <code>part.Size = Vector3.new(5,5,5)</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Script timeout: exhausted allowed execution time</code></td><td>A loop with no yield</td><td>Add <code>task.wait()</code> inside your <code>while true do</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Expected ':' not '.' calling member function</code></td><td>Used a dot where a colon belongs</td><td><code>part:Destroy()</code>, not <code>part.Destroy()</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X is not a valid member of Y</code></td><td>That child or property doesn't exist</td><td>Check spelling and capitalization in Explorer. It's case-sensitive.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Players.X.PlayerGui.&hellip; is not a valid member</code></td><td>Client ran before the GUI replicated</td><td>Use <code>:WaitForChild()</code> in LocalScripts.</td></tr><tr><td><code>attempt to index a nil value (field 'leaderstats')</code></td><td>leaderstats doesn't exist for that player</td><td>Check the folder is named exactly <code>leaderstats</code> and created on PlayerAdded.</td></tr><tr><td>Nothing happens, no error at all</td><td>The script never ran</td><td>Wrong script type for its location, the script is Disabled, or you set no Parent on a new Instance.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="bh">Debugging checklist</h3><ul class="bl"><li>Is the <b>Output window open</b>? Half of all "no error" reports are an unread error.</li><li>Is the script the <b>right type</b> for where it lives? (Episode 1 table.)</li><li>Is <code>Disabled</code> ticked in the script's Properties?</li><li>Add <code>print("reached line 12")</code> at several points to see how far execution gets.</li><li>Print the suspicious variable itself: <code>print("part is:", part)</code>. If it says nil, you found it.</li><li>Check spelling and <b>capitalization</b> against Explorer &mdash; Luau is case-sensitive.</li><li>Did you set <code>Parent</code> on anything you created with <code>Instance.new</code>?</li><li>Are you editing while the game is running? Press Stop first.</li><li>Set a <b>breakpoint</b> by clicking the gutter next to a line number, then Play and step through.</li></ul></div></div></article>
<article class="card apx" id="epD" data-n="D" data-search="d where to go after episode 19 the series stops here. this is the shortest path from beginner to shipping a real game. next advanced roadmap the order to learn things in next what it unlocks difficulty modulescripts reusable code shared across scripts. stop copy-pasting. easy remoteevents / remotefunctions client and server talking. required for any real game. medium guis and udim2 menus, shops, huds, health bars. medium tweenservice smooth animation of anything: doors, ui, cameras. easy datastoreservice saving player data between sessions. medium runservice per-frame code: heartbeat, renderstepped. easy collectionservice tag many objects and script them all at once. easy raycasting guns, line-of-sight, ground detection. medium userinputservice / contextactionservice keyboard, mouse, mobile, gamepad input. medium metatables &amp; oop building your own classes. hard parallel luau actors and multithreading for heavy work. hard modulescript, the very next thing -- modulescript in replicatedstorage, named &quot;utils&quot; local utils = {} function utils.formattime(seconds) local m = math.floor(seconds / 60) local s = seconds % 60 return string.format(&quot;%02d:%02d&quot;, m, s) end function utils.round(n, places) local mult = 10 ^ (places or 0) return math.floor(n * mult + 0.5) / mult end return utils -- a modulescript must return something -- any other script local replicatedstorage = game:getservice(&quot;replicatedstorage&quot;) local utils = require(replicatedstorage:waitforchild(&quot;utils&quot;)) print(utils.formattime(125)) --&gt; 02:05 a modulescript runs its code once , the first time it&#x27;s required, and every later require gets the exact same returned table back. that makes modules a natural place for shared state. tweenservice in 6 lines local tweenservice = game:getservice(&quot;tweenservice&quot;) local part = script.parent local info = tweeninfo.new(2, enum.easingstyle.quad, enum.easingdirection.out) local goal = {position = part.position + vector3.new(0, 20, 0), transparency = 0.5} tweenservice:create(part, info, goal):play() habits worth building now never trust the client. validate everything on the server, always. name things clearly. playercoins beats pc every time. one script, one job. a 500-line script is many scripts wearing a trenchcoat. use modulescripts early. the moment you copy-paste a function, extract it. disconnect what you connect. leaked connections are the top memory leak. wrap datastore and http calls in pcall . networks fail. read the error, then read the line number. it&#x27;s almost always exactly right. official references roblox creator documentation — the authoritative source for every class, property, and method. engine api reference — look up any object to see everything it can do. luau language docs — the language itself, including types. roblox developer forum — where to ask when you&#x27;re stuck."><header class="chead"><label class="done"><input type="checkbox" class="dchk"><span></span></label><button class="ctoggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="badge apxb">D</span><span class="ctitles"><span class="ctitle">Where to go after episode 19</span><span class="ctag">The series stops here. This is the shortest path from beginner to shipping a real game.</span></span><span class="cmeta">reference</span><span class="caret" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span></button></header><div class="cbody"><div class="cinner"><div class="chips"><span class="chip">next</span><span class="chip">advanced</span><span class="chip">roadmap</span></div><h3 class="bh">The order to learn things in</h3><div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Next</th><th>What it unlocks</th><th>Difficulty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>ModuleScripts</b></td><td>Reusable code shared across scripts. Stop copy-pasting.</td><td>Easy</td></tr><tr><td><b>RemoteEvents / RemoteFunctions</b></td><td>Client and server talking. Required for any real game.</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td><b>GUIs and UDim2</b></td><td>Menus, shops, HUDs, health bars.</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td><b>TweenService</b></td><td>Smooth animation of anything: doors, UI, cameras.</td><td>Easy</td></tr><tr><td><b>DataStoreService</b></td><td>Saving player data between sessions.</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td><b>RunService</b></td><td>Per-frame code: Heartbeat, RenderStepped.</td><td>Easy</td></tr><tr><td><b>CollectionService</b></td><td>Tag many objects and script them all at once.</td><td>Easy</td></tr><tr><td><b>Raycasting</b></td><td>Guns, line-of-sight, ground detection.</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td><b>UserInputService / ContextActionService</b></td><td>Keyboard, mouse, mobile, gamepad input.</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td><b>Metatables & OOP</b></td><td>Building your own classes.</td><td>Hard</td></tr><tr><td><b>Parallel Luau</b></td><td>Actors and multithreading for heavy work.</td><td>Hard</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="bh">ModuleScript, the very next thing</h3><div class="codewrap"><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button><pre class="code"><code><span class="c-com">-- ModuleScript in ReplicatedStorage, named "Utils"</span>
<span class="c-kw">local</span> Utils <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-op">{}</span>

<span class="c-kw">function</span> Utils<span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">formatTime</span><span class="c-op">(</span>seconds<span class="c-op">)</span>
	<span class="c-kw">local</span> m <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">math</span><span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">floor</span><span class="c-op">(</span>seconds <span class="c-op">/</span> <span class="c-num">60</span><span class="c-op">)</span>
	<span class="c-kw">local</span> s <span class="c-op">=</span> seconds <span class="c-op">%</span> <span class="c-num">60</span>
	<span class="c-kw">return</span> <span class="c-api">string</span><span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">format</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-str">"%02d:%02d"</span><span class="c-op">,</span> m<span class="c-op">,</span> s<span class="c-op">)</span>
<span class="c-kw">end</span>

<span class="c-kw">function</span> Utils<span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">round</span><span class="c-op">(</span>n<span class="c-op">,</span> places<span class="c-op">)</span>
	<span class="c-kw">local</span> mult <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-num">10</span> <span class="c-op">^</span> <span class="c-op">(</span>places <span class="c-kw">or</span> <span class="c-num">0</span><span class="c-op">)</span>
	<span class="c-kw">return</span> <span class="c-api">math</span><span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">floor</span><span class="c-op">(</span>n <span class="c-op">*</span> mult <span class="c-op">+</span> <span class="c-num">0.5</span><span class="c-op">)</span> <span class="c-op">/</span> mult
<span class="c-kw">end</span>

<span class="c-kw">return</span> Utils      <span class="c-com">-- a ModuleScript MUST return something</span></code></pre></div><div class="codewrap"><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button><pre class="code"><code><span class="c-com">-- any other script</span>
<span class="c-kw">local</span> <span class="c-api">ReplicatedStorage</span> <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">game</span><span class="c-op">:</span><span class="c-fn">GetService</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-str">"ReplicatedStorage"</span><span class="c-op">)</span>
<span class="c-kw">local</span> Utils <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">require</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-api">ReplicatedStorage</span><span class="c-op">:</span><span class="c-fn">WaitForChild</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-str">"Utils"</span><span class="c-op">))</span>

<span class="c-api">print</span><span class="c-op">(</span>Utils<span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">formatTime</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-num">125</span><span class="c-op">))</span>   <span class="c-com">--&gt; 02:05</span></code></pre></div><div class="callout tip"><span class="ci">&#9733;</span><div>A ModuleScript runs its code <b>once</b>, the first time it's required, and every later <code>require</code> gets the exact same returned table back. That makes modules a natural place for shared state.</div></div><h3 class="bh">TweenService in 6 lines</h3><div class="codewrap"><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button><pre class="code"><code><span class="c-kw">local</span> <span class="c-api">TweenService</span> <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">game</span><span class="c-op">:</span><span class="c-fn">GetService</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-str">"TweenService"</span><span class="c-op">)</span>
<span class="c-kw">local</span> part <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">script</span><span class="c-op">.</span>Parent

<span class="c-kw">local</span> info <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-api">TweenInfo</span><span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">new</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-num">2</span><span class="c-op">,</span> <span class="c-api">Enum</span><span class="c-op">.</span>EasingStyle<span class="c-op">.</span>Quad<span class="c-op">,</span> <span class="c-api">Enum</span><span class="c-op">.</span>EasingDirection<span class="c-op">.</span>Out<span class="c-op">)</span>
<span class="c-kw">local</span> goal <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-op">{</span>Position <span class="c-op">=</span> part<span class="c-op">.</span>Position <span class="c-op">+</span> <span class="c-api">Vector3</span><span class="c-op">.</span><span class="c-fn">new</span><span class="c-op">(</span><span class="c-num">0</span><span class="c-op">,</span> <span class="c-num">20</span><span class="c-op">,</span> <span class="c-num">0</span><span class="c-op">),</span> Transparency <span class="c-op">=</span> <span class="c-num">0.5</span><span class="c-op">}</span>

<span class="c-api">TweenService</span><span class="c-op">:</span><span class="c-fn">Create</span><span class="c-op">(</span>part<span class="c-op">,</span> info<span class="c-op">,</span> goal<span class="c-op">):</span><span class="c-fn">Play</span><span class="c-op">()</span></code></pre></div><h3 class="bh">Habits worth building now</h3><ul class="bl"><li><b>Never trust the client.</b> Validate everything on the server, always.</li><li><b>Name things clearly.</b> <code>playerCoins</code> beats <code>pc</code> every time.</li><li><b>One script, one job.</b> A 500-line script is many scripts wearing a trenchcoat.</li><li><b>Use ModuleScripts early.</b> The moment you copy-paste a function, extract it.</li><li><b>Disconnect what you connect.</b> Leaked connections are the top memory leak.</li><li><b>Wrap DataStore and HTTP calls in <code>pcall</code>.</b> Networks fail.</li><li><b>Read the error, then read the line number.</b> It's almost always exactly right.</li></ul><h3 class="bh">Official references</h3><ul class="bl"><li><a href="https://create.roblox.com/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roblox Creator Documentation</a> &mdash; the authoritative source for every class, property, and method.</li><li><a href="https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Engine API Reference</a> &mdash; look up any object to see everything it can do.</li><li><a href="https://luau.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Luau language docs</a> &mdash; the language itself, including types.</li><li><a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roblox Developer Forum</a> &mdash; where to ask when you're stuck.</li></ul></div></div></article>
